From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:28:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gemini): read gemini-cli 0.47's session-*.jsonl record
 stream

0.47 writes chats/session-<ts>-<id8>.jsonl, an append-only record stream;
the adapter listed and read one-document .json files only, so derive and
resolve_main_file saw nothing a 0.47 CLI wrote. ConversationReader now
replays the stream the way gemini-cli's loadConversationRecord does
(metadata merges, messages upsert by id, $set merges or replaces messages,
$rewindTo truncates), and PathResolver lists, resolves and names .jsonl
chat files, a .jsonl twin winning over a same-stem .json.

The goldens pipeline, cross_harness_matrix and real_fixture_roundtrip each
assembled the stream by appending every record, which doubled each
assistant turn (0.47 re-appends a message when its tool calls complete)
and ignored $set. They now call the adapter; the gemini goldens are
recaptured (12 IR steps, not 22; last_activity from the last $set).
tests/jsonl_sessions.rs places the real capture where 0.47 writes it.
Qualifier b0a413e4 and 0b188981 resolved fixed; pipeline anchors
re-recorded. pr/19 records the piece.
